@startuml seq-weaver-weave

title weaver weave — Entity to Output via Go text/template

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444

actor "User" as user
participant "cmd/" as cmd
participant "weave/" as weave
participant "stdin" as stdin
participant "Filesystem" as fs

== Flag parsing (currently broken) ==

user -> cmd : weaver weave -t <template>\n[-e <entity>] [-o <output>]
cmd --> user : unknown flag error on stderr, exit 1\n(flags are registered inside the Run\nfunction, after Cobra has parsed argv)

== Intended weave flow ==

user -> cmd : weaver weave (flag-less invocation\nreaches Run)
cmd -> cmd : register -t/-e/-o flags and\nMarkFlagRequired("template")\n— both too late to take effect
cmd -> fs : os.Open(entity path)\nwhen -e is set
cmd -> fs : os.Create(output path) when -o is set\n(truncates an existing file, no prompt)
cmd -> weave : New(templatePath, input, output).Do()
weave -> fs : template.ParseFiles(templatePath)
weave -> stdin : io.ReadAll(input)\n(stdin by default, entity file with -e)
weave -> weave : parseData — JSON array first,\nthen YAML sequence of maps
loop each data item
  weave -> fs : tmpl.Execute(output, item)\n(stdout by default, file with -o)
end
weave --> cmd : nil or error
cmd --> user : rendered text on stdout

== Errors ==

user -> cmd : template missing / bad data /\nempty data set
cmd --> user : "Weave process failed: <error>"\nprinted — but exit 0 (Run, not RunE)

@enduml
